v0.10.19: REAL/f64 aggregates + agents.updated_at — two drift families closed

NOTE: also carries mig-166 (agents.updated_at), authored for a
v0.10.18 hotfix. That number went to an unrelated console updater
fix from a parallel session, so mig-166 ships here with mig-167.
References below to v0.10.18 as already-shipped mean "this release".

Mo hit this in the Resolve Forecast modal (Alcaraz US Open 2026):

  Server error: error occurred while decoding column 0: mismatched
  types; Rust type `f64` (as SQL type `FLOAT8`) is not compatible
  with SQL type `FLOAT4`

Same shape as v0.10.15/16/18 (owner_id/updated_at column drift),
different axis: numeric precision instead of column existence.

  * fermi_forecasts.brier_score is REAL (mig-048).
  * resolve_forecast() returns REAL (mig-094).
  * MIN(REAL) / MAX(REAL) return REAL.
  * AVG(REAL) / STDDEV(REAL) widen to DOUBLE PRECISION.

sqlx enforces exact SQL↔Rust type match. Every site binding f64
against a REAL column 400s. AVG/STDDEV happened to work because
Postgres widened; MIN/MAX and resolve_forecast() did not.

Why now: forecast resolution requires auth + RBAC + non-admin FK
realignment + owner check. Every gate before v0.10.15 masked
this. Mo's account is clean end-to-end after v0.10.9→v0.10.13,
so his click is the first request to reach the decoding step.

Substrate rule (v0.10.19 onwards):

  Every numeric aggregate or scalar-returning SQL function
  published to Rust returns DOUBLE PRECISION — naturally
  (AVG/STDDEV) or by explicit ::float8 cast (MIN/MAX,
  resolve_forecast). Rust reads f64. No f32 in the read path.

Changes:

  handlers/forecasts.rs (4 sites)
    * resolve_forecast_handler:  SELECT resolve_forecast(...)::float8
    * portfolio_stats_handler:   MIN/MAX ::float8 (parens for prec.)
    * my_stats_handler:          MIN/MAX ::float8
    * leaderboard_handler:       MIN/MAX ::float8 in fallback branch

  migrations/167_fermi_leaderboard_float8_minmax.sql
    * DROP + recreate materialized view with ::float8 on MIN/MAX
    * CREATE OR REPLACE doesn't exist for matviews — column types
      are fixed at creation, so drop is unavoidable.
    * CASCADE takes indexes; recreated after WITH DATA rebuild.
    * Idempotent, PgBouncer-safe DO blocks, RAISE NOTICE
      observability, post-migration column-type assertion.

  src/api_server.rs
    * Registers mig-167. test_all_migrations_registered passes.

The three drift families, all now closed:

  v0.10.15  agents.owner_id (never existed)   eval_brier.rs
  v0.10.16  agents.owner_id (never existed)   fork.rs
  v0.10.18  agents.updated_at (mig-166 adds)  publish_pipeline+lifecycle
  v0.10.19  REAL vs f64 on aggregates         forecasts.rs + mig-167

Elevates v0.11.0 trust-contract from "blocking on spec" to "start
immediately, spec inline." Four consecutive hotfixes shipping the
same underlying invariant is enough evidence.

(v0.10.17 was Ivan's parallel Activity-panel work, unrelated.)

Not in scope: general audit of every REAL column across the DB.
The four sites here are covered by direct evidence + code review;
others (forecast_commitments, confidence_interval_low/high,
sim_probability) need the v0.11.0 substrate to sweep properly.

Related:
  mig-048   fermi_forecasts REAL columns declared
  mig-094   resolve_forecast() + fermi_leaderboard defined
  v0.10.13  text=uuid family (row-type drift)
  v0.10.18  column-existence drift, mig-166
